WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.697
Microsoft Learn's page, Configure a
Logic App for Lifecycle Workflow use,

2
00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:07.563
gives the definition to
paste into code view.

3
00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:10.747
It's Microsoft's only sample
for this integration,

4
00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:14.787
so the repository pins the page,
from the entra docs repository.

5
00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:18.237
Running the definition against
fakes shows what it leaves to you.

6
00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:21.317
It resumes the task with
the Logic App's managed

7
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:24.238
identity and no secret,
and the kit keeps that.

8
00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:28.451
But it hard-codes the worldwide
Graph host, and calls back on beta.

9
00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:30.919
It uses the callback path as it arrives,

10
00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:35.625
so any path appended to the Graph host
gets a POST with the identity's token.

11
00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:40.050
It always reports completed, so a
failed revocation reads as done.

12
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.539
If work you add before the callback fails,

13
00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:46.125
no callback is sent, and the task
waits out the whole timeout.

14
00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:47.863
It has no idempotency.

15
00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:51.699
And it carries the subject's
name and email into run history.

16
00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:54.694
The verdict: the right
shape and the right trigger,

17
00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:58.250
but not safe to run as the
leaver's revocation as published.
